---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
const guide = {
  "title": "US F-1 Student Visa from Pakistan: I-20, SEVIS & Interview",
  "description": "Plan a US student visa application around the chosen school, I-20, SEVIS, DS-160 and the official interview process.",
  "intro": "Plan a US student visa application around the chosen school, I-20, SEVIS, DS-160 and the official interview process.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Department of State student visas",
      "url": "https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/us-visas/study/student-visa.html"
    },
    {
      "title": "ICE SEVIS I-901",
      "url": "https://www.ice.gov/sevis/i901"
    },
    {
      "title": "Official interview wait times",
      "url": "https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/us-visas/visa-information-resources/global-visa-wait-times.html"
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Start with school acceptance",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Check the school is SEVP-approved and obtain the appropriate I-20 after acceptance. The institution records you in SEVIS. Academic and vocational routes differ; a visitor visa is not the ordinary route for a US degree."
      ],
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "heading": "Keep the fees separate",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The published F-1 application fee is USD 185. SEVIS I-901 is a separate fee with its own rules: check ICE’s current schedule and payment instructions. Confirm other applicable charges rather than treating one payment as the total."
      ],
      "source": 1
    },
    {
      "heading": "Build a useful evidence file",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Complete DS-160 and follow the responsible embassy’s appointment instructions. Keep the I-20, passport, confirmation, receipts and requested supporting papers accessible. School, course and identity details must agree.",
        "Create a funding table separating tuition, living and travel costs. Explain each funding source. A sponsorship letter alone does not explain access to funds or how the remaining costs will be covered."
      ],
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "heading": "Prepare for the interview",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Be ready to explain course choice, academic preparation and funding naturally. Use the official wait tool for the post/category. Appointment availability and administrative processing vary; do not interpret a suggested date as a promised outcome."
      ],
      "source": 2
    },
    {
      "heading": "Check the travel conditions",
      "paragraphs": [
        "New student visas can be issued up to 365 days before the course starts, but new students cannot enter on them more than 30 days before the start. If dates change, coordinate with the school. Employment and practical training require the relevant authorisation; a student visa is not general work permission."
      ],
      "source": 0
    }
  ]
};
---
<GuideLayout {...guide} />
